---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import { IDENTITY } from '../data/identity';
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const normalizedBase = baseUrl.endsWith('/') ? baseUrl : `${baseUrl}/`;
const withBase = (href: string) => href.startsWith('http') || href.startsWith('mailto:') || href.startsWith('#') ? href : `${normalizedBase}${href.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
const portraitUrl = withBase('/images/carlos-jorques-intro.webp');
---

<Layout title={`About ${IDENTITY.name} | ${IDENTITY.primaryTitle}`} description="Meet Carlos Jorques, a curious engineer and technical leader connecting control, embedded software, and teams around intelligent physical systems.">
	<div class="about-page">
		<section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
			<p class="about-eyebrow">About me</p>
			<div class="about-hero__layout">
				<div class="about-hero__copy">
					<h1 id="about-title">I’m a curious engineer and technical leader connecting control, embedded software, and teams around intelligent physical systems.</h1>
					<p class="about-hero__lead">I’m {IDENTITY.name}, an <strong>{IDENTITY.primaryTitle}</strong>. My early curiosity about electronics and robotics kept bringing me back to a simple question with a complicated answer: <strong>how does a robot even know what to do?</strong> That question led me into a career in automatic control research, production embedded systems, and technical leadership.</p>
					<p class="about-hero__lead">Today, I see the answer to that question broader than just making a machine act intelligently. People and organisations must be able to understand, trust, and rely on how it provides solutions. Ultimately, {IDENTITY.purpose} </p>
					<nav class="about-hero__actions" aria-label="About quick links">
						<a href={withBase('/cv/')}>View CV</a>
						<a href={withBase('/work/')}>Selected work</a>
						<a href={withBase('/contact/')}>Contact</a>
					</nav>
				</div>
				<figure class="about-portrait-frame">
					<img class="about-portrait" src={portraitUrl} alt="Carlos Jorques" width="768" height="1024" loading="eager" decoding="async" />
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="editorial-section" id="background" aria-label="Where that question took me">
			<div class="section-rail"><p>Where that question took me</p></div>
			<div class="story-block">
				<p>My professional experience is rooted in the automotive industry, working with international teams at Scania, Volvo CE, and MAHLE Electronics across electrified, autonomous, and heavy-duty vehicles. I connect physical behaviour and uncertainty with control algorithms, embedded implementation, and validation. As a technical leader, I turn complex system needs into clear decisions about behaviour, architecture, interfaces, and validation, while helping engineers understand how their work fits into the whole system.</p>
				<p>Curiosity still shapes how I work: understand the system, explore alternatives, test ideas, be willing to try something new, and keep learning. Along the way, that approach has contributed to patents and scientific publications.That belief guides how I approach engineering, lead teams, and decide which ideas are worth pursuing. </p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="editorial-section" id="approach" aria-label="How I approach difficult problems">
			<div class="section-rail"><p>How I approach difficult problems</p></div>
			<div class="story-block">
				<p>I like difficult problems, but I do not assume they need complicated solutions. I start by asking what the system must do, what the physics allow, what the measurements can actually tell us, and what happens when something goes wrong. Models, simulations, software tests, and experiments help me challenge the answer.</p>
				<p>Testing on hardware is good at exposing assumptions. When results differ from expectations, I would rather revisit the model, implementation, and interfaces before adding complexity. A solution is only good if the team can understand it, validate it, and maintain it.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="editorial-section" id="collaboration" aria-label="Making difficult things understandable">
			<div class="section-rail"><p>Making difficult things understandable</p></div>
			<div class="story-block">
				<p>When a technical problem becomes tangled, I often start by drawing it. Diagrams, plots, and concrete examples make behaviour, interfaces, and unknowns easier to see. That habit comes partly from years of teaching and mentoring, and it has become central to how I lead.</p>
				<p>I do not think technical leadership means having every answer. It means asking useful questions, giving people enough context, making decisions when needed, and helping engineers take ownership of their work. I want people to understand why a decision was made and feel able to challenge it with better evidence.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="editorial-section" id="beyond-engineering" aria-label="Away from engineering">
			<div class="section-rail"><p>Away from engineering</p></div>
			<div class="story-block">
				<p>Outside work, basketball gives me a different kind of team challenge and a way to switch off. I also enjoy making things, from electronics and home automation to 3D printing, lamps, and painting. Time with my partner, our child, our dog, and friends keeps work in perspective. Not every experiment needs a business case; sometimes making something for fun and curiosity is enough.</p>
			</div>
		</section>


		<section class="section about-closing" aria-label="Contact">
			<ContactCTA
				title="See how this thinking shows up in practice."
				body="If you want to discuss a project, a role, or a technical challenge, I’d be happy to talk."
				primaryHref="/work/"
				primaryLabel="View Selected Work"
				secondaryHref="/cv/"
				secondaryLabel="View CV"
				tertiaryHref="/contact/?source=about#message-title"
				tertiaryLabel="Contact"
				sourceSection="about-closing"
				ctaIdPrefix="about-closing"
			/>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-page { width:min(calc(100% - 5rem),var(--content-width)); margin:0 auto; padding:0; }
	.about-eyebrow { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:.82rem; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:.08em; line-height:1.4; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--color-muted); }
	.about-hero { padding:clamp(3rem,5vw,4.6rem) 0 0; }
	.about-eyebrow { margin:0; }
	.about-hero__layout { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.35fr) minmax(15rem,20rem); gap:2.5rem; align-items:start; margin:1rem 0 5rem; }
	.about-hero__copy { display:grid; gap:1rem; align-content:start; }
	.about-hero h1 { max-width:none; margin:0; font-size:clamp(2.6rem,3.8vw,3.5rem); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-.05em; line-height:1.02; }
	.about-hero__lead { max-width:52rem; margin:0 0 1.15rem; font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--color-text); }
	.about-hero__lead:last-of-type { margin-bottom:0; }
	.about-hero__lead strong { font-weight:700; }
	.about-hero__actions { display:none; }
	.about-story { display:grid; gap:1rem; margin:0; max-width:52rem; }
	.about-story p,.story-block p { margin:0; font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--color-text); }
	.about-portrait-frame { align-self:start; width:100%; aspect-ratio:3 / 4; margin:0; overflow:hidden; border-radius:1.5rem; }
	.about-portrait { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; aspect-ratio:3 / 4; border-radius:1.5rem; box-shadow:0 18px 40px rgba(23,23,23,.08); }
	.editorial-section { display:grid; grid-template-columns:16rem minmax(0,1fr); gap:0; padding:1rem 0 clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem); border-top:1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top:2rem; }
	.editorial-section--with-bottom-border { border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.section-rail { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:.82rem; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:.08em; line-height:1.4; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--color-muted); padding-top:.25rem; }
	.section-rail p { margin:0; max-width:none; color:inherit; font:inherit; letter-spacing:inherit; text-transform:inherit; }
	.story-block { display:grid; gap:.8rem; max-width:52rem; }
	.story-block p { max-width:none; margin:0; font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--color-text); }
	.story-block a { color:var(--color-link); text-underline-offset:.2em; }
	.about-closing { padding:5rem 0; }

	.about-closing .story-block { grid-column:1 / -1; }
	#approach { margin-top:0; }
	@media(max-width:1100px){.about-hero__layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about-portrait-frame{width:min(100%,16rem)}}
	@media(max-width:720px){.about-hero{padding:3rem 0 0}.about-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.15rem,10vw,2.45rem);line-height:1.04}.about-hero__actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem 1rem;margin-top:0}.about-hero__actions a{color:var(--color-link);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600;text-underline-offset:.2em}.editorial-section{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about-hero__lead,.about-story p,.story-block p{font-size:1.05rem}.button{width:100%}}
	@media(max-width:640px){.about-page{width:min(calc(100% - 32px),var(--content-width))}}
</style>
